{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrQFga6msgHekp3j8iSf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019GNaqH8RdxVP6JQexdkqus","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","symbol":"UsersService.create","start_line":29,"end_line":130,"explanation":"Probable cause. The provider is resolved here when a user is created. If the default is wrong (for example `AuthProvidersEnum.google` instead of `?? AuthProvidersEnum.email`), every email-registered user is saved with provider 'google'. `validateLogin` then rejects them with `needLoginViaProvider:google`. Line range is an estimate."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":200,"end_line":232,"explanation":"Second candidate. `register` calls `usersService.create`. If it passes a provider explicitly and passes the wrong one, the user is stored as a google user. It should pass `AuthProvidersEnum.email` or leave the provider unset. Line range is an estimate."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateLogin","start_line":42,"end_line":97,"explanation":"This is where the 422 `needLoginViaProvider:${user.provider}` is raised. It fires when `user.provider !== AuthProvidersEnum.email`. If the comparison or the value it's checked against is wrong, valid email users are rejected. This is less likely than a wrongly stored provider. Line range is an estimate."}],"fix":{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","description":"In `UsersService.create`, make the provider default to `AuthProvidersEnum.email` (`provider: createUserDto.provider ?? AuthProvidersEnum.email`). In `AuthService.register`, don't pass any other provider value. Existing users saved with the wrong provider will need a data fix."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache